# `frontend/src/components/` — reusable UI components (v2)

Shared, presentational components composed by feature pages. No route/data-fetching logic
beyond small self-contained hooks.

## Folder convention (one folder per component)

Each component is `frontend/src/components/<Name>/` containing:
- `<Name>.tsx` — the component.
- `<Name>.css` — its styles (BEM, scoped by a component root class).
- `<Name>.md` — short context doc (purpose, props, behavior, gotchas). **Add/update this
  when you add or change a component.**
- `index.ts` — the public re-export (import via `../components/<Name>`, not deep paths).
- Optional `.cursorrules` for components with non-obvious rules (e.g. `FoilCard`,
  `AppBackground`, `LegalityErrorsPopover`).

## Conventions

- **CSS:** BEM class names rooted at a unique component class; keep styles in the component's
  `.css`. Use design tokens from `src/styles/tokens.css` — no hardcoded colors/spacing where a
  token exists. Update `STYLE_GUIDE_V2.md` when you change a visual pattern.
- **z-index:** popovers/tooltips/menus that must sit above page content use **9999** (matches
  the global-nav rule). See `LegalityErrorsPopover`, `ProfileMenu`, `UserMenu`.
- **Responsive:** never branch on user-agent. Use `useLayoutMode()` and
  `.layout-mobile` / `.layout-desktop` scoped CSS.
- **Card images:** never hardcode image paths — use the `CardImage` component / `cardImages`
  helpers so the CDN base + thumbnail rules apply.
- **Data:** components stay presentational; pass data/handlers via props. Small read hooks
  using the shared `lib/api` client + React Query are fine, but prefer lifting fetches to the
  feature page.
- Keep accessibility in mind: focus management for popovers/menus, `aria-*` on toggles,
  keyboard close (Esc) for overlays.
